# Adopt-First (discovery before scaffold)

Before inventing modules, services, or substantial new code, **search then decide**. Full runbook: `docs/CURSOR_ERP_SAAS_SETUP_GUIDE.md`.

## Mandatory order (skip only for tiny in-file fixes)

1. **In-repo** — `docs/decisions/`, existing packages/apps, claude-mem / prior plans.
2. **Skills** — project `.cursor/skills/` → [skills.sh](https://skills.sh/) / `npx skills find <query>` → install only after license + exclusion check.
3. **MCP** — [awesome-mcp-servers](https://github.com/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers) / Glama; prefer read-only; do not mass-enable.
4. **Buy / API / OSS** — GitHub topics, SaaS APIs, satellite compose — prefer **Buy → Integrate → Fork → Build**.
5. **Only then invent** — thin adapters; keep system of record; write a short discovery note in the plan or PR.

## Decision shorthand

| Path | When |
|------|------|
| **Buy** | Commodity (auth, email, payments, flags, analytics) with acceptable lock-in |
| **Integrate** | OSS/SaaS as satellite or library; you own the adapter |
| **Fork** | Need durable control of an MIT/Apache base; budget upstream merge cost |
| **Build** | Differentiator, hard exclusions, or no fit after honest search |

## Hard stops (GTR — never “discover into”)

- No ZIMRA / FDMS / fiscalisation / payroll-tax skills, MCP, or modules.
- Bridge-First: no HTML5/WebView QR, printer, biometric, or GPS shortcuts.
- Do not rebase the system of record onto ERPNext/Odoo mid-project.
- Do not auto-install every skill or every MCP server.
